## Question 4: Find Restaurants in Cities with an Average Rating Above 4.0

### Sample Table: ZomatoRestaurants

| id | name | city | rating |
|---:|---|---|---:|
| 1 | Spice Garden | Mumbai | 4.5 |
| 2 | Food Palace | Mumbai | 4.3 |
| 3 | Tasty Bites | Delhi | 3.8 |
| 4 | Royal Kitchen | Delhi | 4.0 |
| 5 | Green Bowl | Pune | 4.6 |
| 6 | Urban Cafe | Pune | 4.4 |

### SQL Query

```sql
WITH CityAverages AS (
    SELECT city, AVG(rating) AS average_rating
    FROM ZomatoRestaurants
    GROUP BY city
)
SELECT
    z.id,
    z.name,
    z.city,
    z.rating
FROM ZomatoRestaurants z
JOIN CityAverages c
    ON z.city = c.city
WHERE c.average_rating > 4.0;
```

### Result Output

| id | name | city | rating |
|---:|---|---|---:|
| 1 | Spice Garden | Mumbai | 4.5 |
| 2 | Food Palace | Mumbai | 4.3 |
| 5 | Green Bowl | Pune | 4.6 |
| 6 | Urban Cafe | Pune | 4.4 |

**Explanation:** Mumbai's average rating is 4.4 and Pune's is 4.5. Delhi's average is 3.9, so restaurants in Delhi are excluded.

